that wait as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/YubiOTP\/Status\/waitingForUser(cancel:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" so a caller can prompt and offer to give up; when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no such feedback is needed, read ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/YubiOTP\/StatusStream\/value","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A touch-triggered slot only works over the OTP keyboard transport, which polls","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the key — the pending touch shows up on every report, and the host can abort between polls.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Over SmartCard the YubiOTP application refuses the command outright with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0x6985"},{"text":" rather than","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"waiting, so the stream yields ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/YubiOTP\/Status\/finished(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" alone and cancellation does"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing. Python and Java accept the same parameters on their SmartCard backends and likewise"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ignore them."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is a limitation of the application, not of SmartCard: an application that defines a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"continuation on top of APDUs can report progress and be cancelled over the same transport."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"CTAP2 does exactly that — it answers "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0x9100"},{"type":"text","text":" and t